  "title": "osf verify becomes a moon-driven checkpoint runner",
  "summary": "`osf verify` stops running checks in-process and becomes a checkpoint runner: it selects this repository's moon tasks by tag (`osf-hook`, `osf-pre-commit`, `osf-pre-push`, `osf-pull-request`), hands moon the affected file list, reads moon's run report back, and journals one hash-chained verification event per task plus a checkpoint-complete event. A new `osf check <name>` command exposes each individual check (scan, scan-staged, lint-writing, lint-skill, scan-commits) so a moon task can run it alone and write SARIF; `osf hook post-tool` runs the hook checkpoint on the file an agent just wrote and refuses the write on an error. Alongside it, git calls are made hermetic against an inherited `GIT_DIR`/`GIT_INDEX_FILE`, `osf hooks install` writes hook scripts outside the repository and points `core.hooksPath` at them, and moon is pinned into the devcontainer and CI.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
